/-!
# Countably many families of relative equivalences

Let `K` be a field. This file carries out the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0G0Y]: there is a countable
set `I` and, for `i ∈ I`, a scheme `S_i` of finite type over `K`, smooth proper `X_i ⟶ S_i` and
`Y_i ⟶ S_i` and a Fourier-Mukai kernel `M_i` of a relative equivalence from `X_i` to `Y_i` over
`S_i`, such that every pair `(X, Y)` of smooth proper `K`-schemes whose perfect derived
categories are `K`-linearly and exactly equivalent occurs as the pair of fibres
`((X_i)_s, (Y_i)_s)` at a `K`-point `s` of some `S_i`.

## The proof

The source chooses a countable subfield `k ⊂ K`; here the role of `k` is played by the
countable Noetherian ring `R₀ = ℤ[∅] ⊂ K`, the bottom stage of the Noetherian approximation
`AlgebraicGeometry.specAdjoinFinsetDiagram` of `Spec K` by the spectra of the subrings
`ℤ[i] ⊂ K` generated by finite subsets `i ⊂ K`. Every stage `Spec ℤ[i]` is of finite type over
`B = Spec R₀`.

* *The countable set.* By [Stacks, Tag 0G0U] the finite-type schemes over `B` fall into
  countably many isomorphism classes, and between two of them there are countably many
  morphisms. So the triples `(a, b → a, c → a)` of chosen representatives `a, b, c` of
  isomorphism classes, with morphisms over `B`, form a countable type. The index set `I` consists
  of those triples which are isomorphic to some *good* system over `B`: a finite-type `S₀` over
  `B` with smooth proper `X₀, Y₀ ⟶ S₀` carrying a relative-equivalence kernel. For each `i ∈ I`
  one such good system is chosen, and `(S_i, X_i, Y_i, M_i)` is its base change to `K`; the
  kernel base changes by [Stacks, Tag 0G0K]. This proves (1), (2), (3).
* *Property (4).* Given `X, Y` and the equivalence, the input `hkernel` provides a kernel `M`
  of a relative equivalence from `X` to `Y` over `Spec K` (the second paragraph of the source's
  proof). `X ⟶ Spec K` and `Y ⟶ Spec K` are proper and smooth, so they descend, as proper smooth
  morphisms, to a stage `Spec ℤ[j]` ([Stacks, Tag 01ZM], [Stacks, Tag 081F],
  [Stacks, Tag 0C0C]: `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_stage_properSmoothModel`). By
  [Stacks, Tag 0G0L] the kernel descends to some stage `Spec ℤ[i]`, `i ⊇ j`. The resulting good
  system over `B` is isomorphic to one of the triples of representatives, hence to the chosen
  system of some index; the composite `Spec K ⟶ Spec ℤ[i] ≅ S₀` is the `K`-point.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_stage_properSmoothModel` — a proper smooth morphism to the limit of
  a cofiltered system of affine schemes is the base change of a proper smooth morphism to a
  stage.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_countable_relativeEquivalenceKernels_of_hasRelativeKernel` — the
  assembly of [Stacks, Tag 0G0Y] from its inputs.

## Implementation notes

The family members are objects of over categories, in the shape in which [Stacks, Tag 0G0Y] is
stated: `S i : Over (Spec K)`, `X i, Y i : Over (S i).left`, a
`K`-point is a morphism `Over.mk (𝟙 (Spec K)) ⟶ S i` and the fibre at it is a base change.

The main theorem takes as hypotheses `h09RFobj`, `h09RFiso` (the two halves of [Stacks, Tag 09RF]
used by [Stacks, Tag 0G0L], whose other inputs are
`AlgebraicGeometry.diagonalKernelAndConvolutionBaseChange` and, at the Noetherian stages used here,
`AlgebraicGeometry.diagonalKernelAndConvolutionPerfectOfNoetherian`) and `hkernel` (that a
`K`-linear exact equivalence `D_perf(𝒪_X) ≌ D_perf(𝒪_Y)` yields a relative-equivalence kernel over
`Spec K`, which the source proves from [Stacks, Tag 0G0D], [Stacks, Tag 0FYY] and [Stacks, Tag
0G0E]). The input [Stacks, Tag 08IB] of [Stacks, Tag 0G0K] is
`AlgebraicGeometry.derivedBaseChangeIsIsoOnQuasicoherent`. The source assumes `K` algebraically
closed; the argument does not use it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G0Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G0Y)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G0U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G0U)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G0K)
